OL,3,AEmbattled Spanish PM insists no prior
OL,4,Awarnings before Ceuta crisis
OL,5,
OL,6,FSanchez also maintained there was no
OL,7,Fevidence Morocco was behind the mass
OL,8,Fcrossing and there had been "close
OL,9,Fco-ordination" between the two
OL,10,Fcountries.
OL,12,FA Spanish police report has highlighted
OL,13,Fthe "total permissiveness" of Moroccan
OL,14,Fsecurity forces, although senior
OL,15,Fofficials insist it does not point the
OL,16,Ffinger at Rabat.
